    "field": "Solar geoengineering",
    "problem": "The potential for unilateral or regional solar geoengineering to cause significant, unintended, and harmful changes to tropical cyclone frequency is poorly understood, posing a major risk that could undermine global climate policy and cause cross-regional damage.",
    "method": "This paper investigates the effects of hemispheric and global solar geoengineering on tropical cyclone frequency using the HadGEM2-ES climate model, with results corroborated by direct storm tracking, various climate proxy metrics, and a widely used statistical-dynamical downscaling model.",
    "task": "This paper investigates the impacts of hemispheric and global solar geoengineering scenarios on North Atlantic tropical cyclone frequency using a climate model and multiple identification methods to reemphasise concerns regarding unilateral deployments.",
